# Satellite session auth — inherit FLOQR login (always)

Patrons sign in **once** on Search / My Profile / Club Admin. Firebase persistence is shared on this origin. **Deep-linked and embedded pages must reuse that session.** A second “Google sign-in” card is a product bug, not a new login surface.

This failed in production as: parent `patron-portal.html` signed in, child iframe `staff-worksheet.html` showing Google / “Sign in to continue.” Same class of bug as Inbox → `scheduling.html`.

## Hub vs satellite

**Hubs** (allowed to show full FLOQR auth: email / phone / Google / Microsoft):

- `index.html` (Search)
- `patron-portal.html` (My Profile)
- `admin.html` (Club Admin)
- `master-admin.html` (Master Admin)

**Satellites** (must use `FLOQRSessionShell`; never Google-only):

| Page | Typical entry |
|---|---|
| `staff-worksheet.html` | Portal Work Calendar iframe + Inbox confirm |
| `scheduling.html` | Manager portal; worker notify must redirect to Work Calendar |
| `role-request.html` | Service Members / FloqAi |
| `commerce.html` / BartR | Portal store / Search tile |
| `guest-list.html` | Club / Search |
| `mingl-chat.html` / `mingl-gist.html` | Portal / Inbox |
| `pickup.html` / RydR | Search |
| `services.html` | Follow Services |
| `payment-return.html` | Stripe return |
| `promoter-admin.html` | Promoter tools |
| `suprstr-search.html` / `suprstar-preview.html` | SupRstR |

**Exceptions (no patron session UI):** `display.html` / `display2.html` (Xibo), seed/debug/onboarding tools.

When you **create or edit** a satellite, wire the shell **in that same change** even if auth was not the ticket. Do not leave a Google-only gate “for later.”

## Required module

File: `floqr-session-shell.js`  
API: `window.FLOQRSessionShell`

Load **after** `firebase-config.js` and **before** the page app:

```html
<script src="./firebase-config.js?v=…"></script>
<script src="./floqr-session-shell.js?v=s3.0.3"></script>
<script src="./my-satellite-app.js?v=s3.0.3"></script>
```

```html
<div class="card" data-floqr-auth-chrome>
  <button type="button" data-floqr-login-btn>Google sign-in</button>
</div>
```

```js
FLOQRSessionShell.bind({
  auth: firebase.auth(),
  chrome: "[data-floqr-auth-chrome]",
  loginButtons: "[data-floqr-login-btn]",
  statusEl: "#myStatus",
  onUser: user => loadPage(user)
});
```

Standalone (not iframe): Google may remain as **one** option after the shell restores session and finds no user. Copy must say restore FLOQR session / open My Profile — not “Google only.”

## Embed / iframe

1. Portal/admin iframes: `embed=1` on `src` (keep `v=`).
2. Embedded path **must not** call `signInWithPopup`. Shell hides login buttons and links **My Profile & Settings** (`target="_parent"`).
3. Shell adds `floqr-embed-mode` and hides duplicate Back chrome.
4. Prefer rendering inside the portal; if you iframe, the child still uses the shell.

## Deep links (Inbox / Email / SMS)

- Worker confirm → `patron-portal.html?tab=work-calendar&shift=&from=schedule-notify`, not manager `scheduling.html`.
- Opening a notify link **must not** mutate status (pending stays pending until Approve selected).
- Old satellite URLs may redirect into the portal; new links must not invent a second login.

## Forbidden

- Satellite whose only sign-in is Google while FLOQR also has email/phone
- Iframe child showing “Sign in to continue” + Google while the parent is signed in
- Assuming `auth.currentUser` on first paint — wait via `bind` / `waitForUser`
- One-off `if (iframe) hide button` — extend `floqr-session-shell.js`
- Inbox CTA **Open Related ShoutOut** on a non-ShoutOut System Message (use type-aware labels)

## Checklist (new or edited satellite)

- [ ] `floqr-session-shell.js` loaded after firebase-config
- [ ] Auth chrome / login buttons marked (or passed to `bind`)
- [ ] `FLOQRSessionShell.bind({ auth, chrome, loginButtons, statusEl, onUser })`
- [ ] Portal iframes use `embed=1`
- [ ] Embedded path does not `signInWithPopup`
- [ ] Status: restoring session / open My Profile — not Google-only
- [ ] If this is a notify/Inbox landing: already-authenticated hub tab, no confirm-on-click
